.TH MW-REMEMBER 1 "2026-09-06" "MemoryWhale 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-remember \- record a single command run into local MemoryWhale storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-remember
.RI [ --cwd
.IR path ]
.RI [ --exit-code
.IR code ]
.RI [ --stdout
.IR text ]
.RI [ --stderr
.IR text ]
.RI [ --notes
.IR text ]
.B --
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B mw-remember --from-hook
.B claude|rho|cursor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-remember
stores one command run \(em its command and arguments, working directory,
exit code, captured output, and an optional note \(em into the local
MemoryWhale SQLite database. It is the low-level building block used by the
per-command shell hook and can also be called directly from scripts. Nothing
is uploaded.
.PP
Supported hooks store structured command provenance as claude, rho, or cursor.
Manual recording stores NULL, displayed and filtered as terminal. This
producing-agent metadata is separate from source type; both are still command
records.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--cwd " path
Working directory to record (default: the current directory).
.TP
.BI "--exit-code " code
.RB "Exit status of the command. Also accepts " --exit .
.TP
.BI "--stdout " text
Captured standard output to store.
.TP
.BI "--stderr " text
Captured standard error to store.
.TP
.BI "--notes " text
Free-form note attached to the run.
.TP
.BI "--capture-kind " "full|hook"
Capture mode, normally full; hook denotes lightweight shell-hook capture.
.TP
.BI "--from-hook " "claude|rho|cursor"
Read that client's hook JSON object from standard input and record a
supported tool event. Cannot be mixed with manual-recording options or
a command.
Unknown, malformed, or empty payloads are ignored. Once valid hook mode is
selected, parsing/storage failures exit 0 so they cannot block the agent;
invalid CLI arguments can still fail.
.PP
Rho events without command text preserve failed/unavailable status and failure
metadata with a sentinel command, not invented command output. Successful
events without command text are skipped. No Python runtime is required.
.PP
Cursor hook mode records supported local Shell events with cursor provenance.
Enable it explicitly with
.BR "mw integrate cursor --capture" ;
MCP access and optional skill installation are separate integration modes.
.TP
.B --
Everything after this is the command and its arguments.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_HOOK_DIAGNOSTICS
Set to exactly 1 to enable fixed, nonfatal stderr diagnostics for Cursor hook
input and storage failures. Default Cursor hook processing is silent on both
output streams. Diagnostics do not include captured payloads or raw storage
errors and never write to stdout. Other hook clients are unchanged.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mw-remember --cwd "$PWD" --exit-code 0 \\
  --notes "started the dev server" -- npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-serve (1)
